<title>MEXICO: Mexico Feb silver output up, other metals detailed.</title>
<headline>Mexico Feb silver output up, other metals detailed.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico, the world's largest refined silver maker, produced 194,419 kg of silver in February against 193,117 kg in the same month a year earlier, National Statistics Institute (INEGI) said Wednesday.</p>
<p>Other production levels of other metals and minerals are outlined in table form below.  </p>
<p>    Product	 Feb 97     Feb 96    Chng    Jan-Feb</p>
<p>    Gold	    1,890	1,775   6.5 pct     4,088</p>
<p>    Silver	194,419    193,117   0.7 pct   434,373</p>
<p>    Lead	   15,143     12,355  22.5 pct    34,387</p>
<p>    Copper	 23,256     24,354  -4.5 pct    45,159</p>
<p>    Zinc	   30,488     25,465  19.7 pct    61,945</p>
<p>    Coal	  767,653    877,437 -12.5 pct 1,531,933</p>
<p>    Iron	  505,895    541,251  -6.5 pct   962,302</p>
<p>    Sulphur	69,320     78,977 -12.2 pct   144,642</p>
<p>    Dolomite     71,966     71,717   N/A	 132,820</p>
<p>    Gypsum	284,686    275,657   3.3 pct   653,726</p>
<p>    Phosphorite  52,148     54,598   N/A	 105,414</p>
<p>Legend: Precious metals output in kgs. Others in tonnes. Coal output in mineral volume.</p>
<p>((--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530)) E-mail at chris.aspin@reuters.com</p>
